	quests: [
		{
			x: -0.5d
			y: 0.5d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "Darkness or Brightness?!"
			description: [
				"&dHm, seems we got a few choices on where to go next. Four places actually. So we're going to split it into two and two to keep focus."
				""
				"&5Where are we going to start, sis?"
				""
				"&dHmm, Bandit just went through Lelyetia, so lets take a break from the forested places and go somewhere different."
				""
				"&5Yeck, I see. Guess you get to choose which one you start with, Bandit. We'll fork the quest chain here so you can work on either one at your own pace. They are...very different from each other, I have to say."
			]
			dependencies: ["0332B6DA83347AEB"]
			id: "24E1C6762864AEC6"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5A507B2D491199DC"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Choices, Choices"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2ECB7916F9D8A1C3"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "To the Deep Dark"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 3.0d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&dThe Deeplands is the furthest thing you can get from the endless sun of Barathos... well, without it being a fully underwater world."
				""
				"&5Please. Please no water temple..."
				""
				"&dNah, brother. This is the darkest of caves, the Deeplands. You'll need to bring a lot of light of some kind, there is no light from the sky."
				""
				"&5And to get to the Deeplands is easy. Bring some ore, place it on top of, or as close to Bedrock in the Overworld (the bottom most indestructable layer), and mine it while you have a Blank Runestone in your inventory."
				""
				"&dAnd bam, Deeplands Realmstone. Simple, no? Well, if it doesn't work with one ore, try something simple like Iron Ore."
			]
			dependencies: ["24E1C6762864AEC6"]
			id: "20DC9D8BCD99C99E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "52C09B57B2D478E8"
				type: "item"
				item: "aoa3:deeplands_realmstone"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6EF4F8ECEE5179A3"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "To the Endless Sun"
			x: 1.0d
			y: -2.0d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&dBarathos is an endless desert, with a relentless sun."
				""
				"&5A sun that shines even in the deepest cave... yuck."
				""
				"&dRight? But you'll need to explore and fight in Barathos a bit, as it is the home of two of the FOP Corporate Bosses. "
				""
				"&5To get the Barathos Realmstone, you'll need to find a Husk and beat it to death with a Blank Realmstone. As in, getting the killing blow while holding the Realmstone."
				""
				"&dGiven how... badly the FOP have patched and patched and added onto their own game server, Husks might be kind of hard to find. Usually, they spawn in the deserts at night instead of zombies but..."
				""
				"&5Just check out the Shop Tablet if you are having bad luck, Bandit."
			]
			dependencies: ["24E1C6762864AEC6"]
			id: "59965C1CF354E4CE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "266E88C418292731"
				type: "item"
				item: "aoa3:barathos_realmstone"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "78D3EFCF64AA944B"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Land So Bright"
			x: 3.25d
			y: -2.0d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&dBarathos is a wide, barren world."
				""
				"&5It's bright, warm, and mostly empty. But there are, or used to be people living there. They've long since become Power Users, and most of them replaced by FOP NPCs and creatures."
				""
				"&dBut that's just the surface. Underground there is... a lot of rich ore to be found. Part of why the FOP goes after these barren worlds, the underground is less likely to be tapped."
				""
				"&5Full of riches for them to send Users to exploit."
				""
				"&dGo and explore. Most of the place is slightly hilly, but there should be a lot of structures around. I'd mark em all down on your map, you'll probably need to visit most of them."
				""
				"&5Be on your guard. The creatures can be pretty hardy and dangerous."
			]
			dependencies: ["59965C1CF354E4CE"]
			id: "504DC166104A8063"
			tasks: [{
				id: "762CDDE7AAAC7F06"
				type: "dimension"
				title: "Travel to Barathos"
				dimension: "aoa3:barathos"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "35A64F2CA80CFA3F"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Red Lands"
			x: 5.75d
			y: -2.0d
			shape: "pentagon"
			description: [
				"&dUnderground, Barathos is split into two halves."
				""
				"&5The upper 2/3rds is primarily Baron Stone. "
				""
				"&dAnd the last third is Hellstone and Lava. "
				""
				"&5There isn't much variation in the materials that make up the land. There are caves underground, but they might be harder to find. You might want to invest in some Ore searching gear. Scannes or Dousing Rods or something."
				""
				"&dCause you'll need to find the three Ores this world is known for : Baronyte and Varsium ore above Y 25..."
				""
				"&5...and Blazium below Y 25."
			]
